---
number: 426
title: There Is a Song in My Heart
sp_category: "26"
topic: Joy and Peace
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
There is a song in my heart today,
Something I never had;
Jesus has taken my sins away,
O say, but I’m glad!

[chorus]
O say, but I’m glad, I’m glad,
O say, but I’m glad!
Jesus has come and my cup’s overrun,
O say, but I’m glad!

[verse 2]
Wonderful, marvelous love He brings,
Into a heart that’s sad;
Thru darkest tunnels the soul just sings,
O say, but I’m glad!

[chorus]
O say, but I’m glad, I’m glad,
O say, but I’m glad!
Jesus has come and my cup’s overrun,
O say, but I’m glad!

[verse 3]
We have a fellowship rich and sweet,
Tongue can ne’er relate;
Abiding in Him is a real treat,
O say, but it’s great!

[chorus]
O say, but I’m glad, I’m glad,
O say, but I’m glad!
Jesus has come and my cup’s overrun,
O say, but I’m glad!

[verse 4]
Won’t you come to Him with all your care,
Weary and worn and sad?
You, too, will sing as His love you share,
O say, but I’m glad!

[chorus]
O say, but I’m glad, I’m glad,
O say, but I’m glad!
Jesus has come and my cup’s overrun,
O say, but I’m glad!
